      "id": "19410",
      "key": "SFCC-850",
      "summary": "Copy Category Merchandising",
      "description": "As a Site Merchandiser, \n\n\nI want to copy the curated product order from a category in one storefront to a category in another storefront in BM, \n\n\nso that I can use an already-merchandised category as a base for another storefront and make adjustments from there, rather than curating from scratch.\nThis is a custom Business Manager extension replicating a capability Zimmermann has in Magento today. It relates to SFCC-201 which covers OOB category merchandising.\nExample: \nWhen the merchandiser is preparing the latest category for Dresses, they could go and manually curate the AU Dresses category. Then when the move on to the HK Dresses category, they can select the AU Dresses category as a base. This will copy the setup of the AU dresses category (assigned products and their order) into the HK Dresses category. \n\n\nThen the merchandiser has the foundation and will adjust the HK Dresses category if needed (inventory levels will likely differ per storefront so then some products may need to be removed, etc.). ",
