      "id": "19577",
      "key": "SFCC-947",
      "summary": "PDP Size Selector UX & Accessibility (Size Guide Placement + Measmerize)",
      "description": "The Zimmermann team are concerned that without prominent size guide placement, incorrect size selection (currently a key driver of returns) will continue to be an issue. While Measmerize is the preferred solution, low platform adoption means it can't be relied on in the interim. From a UX perspective, if the size guide isn't immediately visible, a user would naturally expect to find it further down the page with the product details, which aligns with its current placement. Vicky is keen to test whether the options are intuitive, and the team haven't yet explored Measmerize to understand what's possible within that flow.\nOur (Tim and myself's) main concerns are about the compromises to accessibility if we were to implement the proposed designs with the links within the dropdown. Essentially….\nAccessibility & Build (Tim can explain this better, but from what I could understand....)\nEmbedding links inside that context can introduce complexity:\nBlur/active state conflict: When a user tabs to or clicks a link, the dropdown may interpret this as an \"on blur\" event and close — meaning the link becomes unreachable and the dropdown dismisses before the user can interact.\nKeyboard navigation: Users navigating by keyboard expect the arrow keys to move between size options. A link in the mix disrupts this pattern and can trap or misdirect focus unexpectedly.\nScreen readers: Mixing interactive link elements within a dropdown can send confusing signals to assistive technology. The change of context triggered by a link (navigating away from the page) is particularly disorienting when a user is mid-task selecting a size and can loose page context\nUX & Repetition\nBeyond the technical concerns, the current design creates a confusing duplication of intent. The \"Recommended: 0P*\" label shown outside the dropdown already links to the size guide, and a \"Find your size\" link then appears again inside the dropdown pointing to the same destination. For screen reader users, this double-up is especially problematic as the sudden change of context (navigating away mid-selection) is hard to anticipate or recover from.\nRecommendation\nWe'd suggest keeping the size guide link external to the dropdown (in the flow here) within the existing accordion (as the \"Size Guide\" drawer already present in the design), and the 'find your size' as a persistent link next to the size selector label, allowing users to easily adjust their details in Measmerize. This keeps the dropdown clean, the interaction predictable, and doesn't compromise accessibility. If still concerned, test the solutions to understand if customers would be able to find size guide, as well as if they would be able to set-up Measmerize and navigate within the flow",
