      "customfield_10231": {
        "value": {
          "type": "doc",
          "version": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1. Given a customer attempts to register with an email address already associated with an existing SFCC account, when they submit the registration form, then the system blocks account creation and displays an inline error prompting them to log in or reset their password."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "2. Given a customer attempts to change their email address in My Account to one already associated with an existing SFCC account, when they submit the change, then the system blocks the update and displays an inline error."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "3. Given a customer registers or logs in using Apple ID with the Hide My Email option, when Apple passes a private relay address to SFCC, then the system checks whether that relay address or the customer's underlying Apple ID is already associated with an existing account."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "4. Given a relay address match is found against an existing account, when the customer authenticates via Apple, then the system links the session to the existing account rather than creating a new one."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "5. Given no match is found for the relay address, when the customer completes registration via Apple, then the system creates a new account using the relay address as the email identifier."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "6. Given a customer has an existing account registered with their real email and subsequently registers via Apple using Hide My Email, when the duplicate is detected, then the system prompts the customer to log in with their existing credentials and link their Apple ID to the existing account rather than creating a new account."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "7. Given a customer account exists with an Apple relay address, when the customer contacts support or attempts account recovery, then the system supports account lookup by Apple ID in addition to email address."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
